{"content":[{"c":["PERDITION*"],"t":"p"},{"c":["Term used eight times in the ","kjv"," NT to express the eternal aspect of the destruction of life and self. In ",{"r":"Phil.1.28","t":"ref","v":"Philippians 1:28"},", “perdition” is the opposite of “salvation.” ",{"r":"Heb.10.39","t":"ref","v":"Hebrews 10:39"}," contrasts it with “preserving one’s soul.” ",{"r":"2Pet.3.7","t":"ref","v":"Second Peter 3:7"}," links perdition with the day of judgment, while ",{"r":"1Tim.6.9","t":"ref","v":"1 Timothy 6:9"}," has both present and future in view. “Son of perdition” is a label affirming the destiny of the betrayer Judas (",{"r":"John.17.12","t":"ref","v":"Jn 17:12"},") and of the antichrist (",{"r":"2Thes.2.3","t":"ref","v":"2 Thes 2:3"},"). In ",{"r":"Rev.17.8,11","t":"ref","v":"Revelation 17:8, 11"}," perdition designates the final abode of the beast. ",{"r":"Rev.19.20","t":"ref","v":"Revelation 19:20"}," and ",{"r":"Rev.20.10","t":"ref","v":"20:10"}," identify this abode as the “lake of fire,” a place of everlasting torment."],"t":"p"},{"c":["“Perdition” occurs four times in the ","rsv"," NT (",{"r":"John.17.12","t":"ref","v":"Jn 17:12"},"; ",{"r":"2Thes.2.3","t":"ref","v":"2 Thes 2:3"},"; ",{"r":"Rev.17.8,11","t":"ref","v":"Rv 17:8, 11"},") and twice in the OT (",{"r":"2Sam.22.5","t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 22:5"},"; ",{"r":"Ps.18.4","t":"ref","v":"Ps 18:4"},"). In the latter, the parallel lines of Hebrew poetry show that perdition is the equivalent of death."],"t":"p"},{"c":[{"t":"em","v":"See also"}," ",{"id":"Antichrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Antichrist"},"; ",{"id":"Death_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Death"},"; ",{"id":"Judgment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Judgment"},"; ",{"id":"LakeofFire_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Lake of Fire"},"."],"t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Perdition","provenance":{"philippiansReferences":["Phil.1.28"],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5faf6ae5f33454ddd89ec4eda89fd9fd43cf78f4c37bf1e5359df201f4606e2e","sourceItemName":"Perdition","sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"title":"Perdition*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}